            {
                "entry_id": "c2426351-09b2-398e-afe6-9ce6c529d738",
                "word": "Seth",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "de",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ca875bc-aa64-37f9-912d-8b03bd060bb4",
                        "entry_id": "c2426351-09b2-398e-afe6-9ce6c529d738",
                        "glosses": [
                            "biblischer männlicher Eigenname; dritter Sohn von Adam und Eva"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "13ea2cbc-42bd-4eb9-875c-5faa29be295e",
                                "sense_id": "2ca875bc-aa64-37f9-912d-8b03bd060bb4",
                                "text": "Von Seth anfangend wird die Nachkommenschaft bis zu Noah wiedergegeben, zu dessen Zeit alle anderen durch die Flut hinweggerafft wurden (1. Mo 5,3-8; 1. Chr 1,1; Lk 3,38)."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "87a3cf16-dd6d-4381-b420-4b7adcd26bf9",
                        "source_entry_id": "c2426351-09b2-398e-afe6-9ce6c529d738",
                        "source_sense_id": "2ca875bc-aa64-37f9-912d-8b03bd060bb4",
                        "source_sense_description": "biblischer männlicher Eigenname Seth",
                        "target_lang_word": "Seth",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Seth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00026711-ca66-3ac6-8d9c-fe05d15dc056",
                                        "entry_id": "602b722e-96a5-3618-ac04-c80c6e012337",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The third son of Adam and Eve."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2700ac42-b73f-482d-a473-bd63dd4ecb90",
                                                "sense_id": "00026711-ca66-3ac6-8d9c-fe05d15dc056",
                                                "text": "And Adam lived an hundred and thirty years, and begat a son in his own likeness, after his image; and called his name Seth:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27ce6d9c-0411-3479-89bd-00fe73e1a941",
                                        "entry_id": "602b722e-96a5-3618-ac04-c80c6e012337",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name from Hebrew."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cbe7791-c911-4256-a98e-9a10da1d5166",
                                                "sense_id": "27ce6d9c-0411-3479-89bd-00fe73e1a941",
                                                "text": "The children suggested names. In his childhood the ones they knew would have been unheard-of (Scott, Ross, Damian, Liam, Seth) or, strangely enough, too old-fashioned for popular use (Joshua, Simon, Jack, George)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c122e97-36a1-448d-bbba-02e6f6924976",
                                                "sense_id": "27ce6d9c-0411-3479-89bd-00fe73e1a941",
                                                "text": "Reps. Seth Moulton, a Democrat from Massachusetts, and Peter Meijer, a Republican from Michigan, said in a joint statement Tuesday that they had traveled to Kabul “to conduct oversight on the mission to evacuate Americans and our allies” and that the trip had been conducted in secret “to minimize the risk and disruption to the people on the ground.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3ed14c5-1ea2-4be0-8254-ea9fb5195dd4",
                                                "sense_id": "27ce6d9c-0411-3479-89bd-00fe73e1a941",
                                                "text": "'David, Seth and Aaron,' said Emma. 'Biblical names. I wonder if either of the parents is religious.' 'Jewish?' said Sam. 'They sound Old Testament to me.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Seth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4c50a6b8-06a2-3868-b5f9-686f0a0d0a48",
                                        "entry_id": "85047488-8060-3021-b387-ff2820d2ce8e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ancient Egyptian god, variously described as the god of chaos, the god of thunder and storms, or the god of destruction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Egyptian"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a3b46c9-21f8-4911-bd2a-02919fa0da98",
                        "source_entry_id": "c2426351-09b2-398e-afe6-9ce6c529d738",
                        "source_sense_id": "2ca875bc-aa64-37f9-912d-8b03bd060bb4",
                        "source_sense_description": "biblischer männlicher Eigenname Seth",
                        "target_lang_word": "Seth",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Seth",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e0513f2-3ff3-36a3-914b-998dc2e5adab",
                                        "entry_id": "2d637345-f4dc-30fa-8576-30b9c0908a5e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fils d’Adam et Ève, frère d’Abel et Caïn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd670c1d-be72-4190-b8fd-bef1b06b9127",
                                                "sense_id": "6e0513f2-3ff3-36a3-914b-998dc2e5adab",
                                                "text": "Adam connut encore sa femme, Ève ; elle enfanta un fils, et l'appela du nom de Seth, car, dit-elle, Dieu m'a donné un autre fils à la place d'Abel, que Caïn a tué. Seth eut aussi un fils, et il l'appela du nom d'Énosh. C'est alors que l'on commença à invoquer le nom de l'Éternel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Seth",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c67bbbfc-866b-37c5-a408-fbd15aa12df5",
                                        "entry_id": "ed77a4fe-04ae-38df-9051-74da7b25b5d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dieu égyptien à la tête d'un animal indéterminé (peut-être un chien ou un oryctérope du Cap)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Divinité"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a67c636-4884-4ef0-83ad-609e868ca6bc",
                                                "sense_id": "c67bbbfc-866b-37c5-a408-fbd15aa12df5",
                                                "text": "Horus le jeune et Seth s’affrontèrent dans un combat terrible, duquel ressortit vainqueur le fils."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Seth",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
